10. Governance Decisions

Governance decisions SHALL include:

Decision authority
Applicable policy
Supporting evidence
Approval record
Timestamp
Audit references

Governance decisions SHALL be recorded as Decision Records.

11. Audit Governance

Governance SHALL preserve:

Governance actions
Policy evaluations
Approval history
Ownership changes
Stewardship changes
Security changes
Lifecycle transitions

Audit records SHALL be immutable.

12. Governance Quality

Governance effectiveness SHALL be evaluated using:

Policy compliance
Ownership completeness
Stewardship coverage
Audit completeness
Validation success
Lifecycle consistency
Traceability
Security compliance

Quality metrics SHALL themselves be governed.

13. Governance Events

Governance MAY generate Canonical Events.

Examples:

Owner Assigned
Policy Updated
Approval Granted
Steward Changed
Object Classified
Object Archived

Governance events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

14. Federation

Governance SHALL support:

Cross-organization ownership
Federated stewardship
Shared governance policies
Delegated approvals
Distributed audit trails

Federation SHALL preserve accountability.

15. Conformance

A governance implementation conforms if it:

Assigns governance roles.
Implements policy-driven governance.
Preserves audit history.
Supports lifecycle governance.
Maintains accountability.
Preserves governance metadata.
Supports federation.
16. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted governance.
Adaptive policy enforcement.
Autonomous stewardship.
Cross-jurisdiction governance.
Self-assessing governance models.
Continuous compliance monitoring.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical governance semantics.

